# Rigid-water-like force field for the constrained NVE validation case.
#
# Units follow the GMD molecular .ff convention (see src/io/config_loader.cpp):
# energies in kcal/mol, distances in Angstrom, angles in degrees.
#
# THE FORCE CONSTANTS ARE DELIBERATELY ZERO.
#
# The bonds and the angle are declared ONLY so that the special-pair map excludes
# every intramolecular non-bonded pair: the two O-H bonds give the 1-2
# exclusions and the H-O-H angle gives the 1-3 exclusion between the hydrogens.
# With k = 0 they contribute no force and no energy, so the molecule -- alone in
# the cell -- is exactly force free. Its geometry is held entirely by the three
# distance constraints, which is what this case exists to validate.
#
# A free rigid body has analytically known motion, so the checks in analyze.py
# compare against conservation laws rather than only against a previous GMD run.
force_field molecular

lj_cutoff 8.0

type 1 O mass 15.9994 epsilon 0.1521 sigma 3.1507 charge 0.0
type 2 H mass 1.0080  epsilon 0.0460 sigma 0.4000 charge 0.0

# Exclusion-only terms; see above.
bond_type 1 k 0.0 r0 0.9572
angle_type 1 k 0.0 theta0 104.52
